text: >-
  Executive Summary

  In Tuesday, 09 September 2025 at 1117, the Fort Huachuca Military Police
  Station was notified by Daniel Head

  CW2/TTF/SWB), of a suspicious individual at Southwest Border Mission
  Headquarters (BLDG #70525). OFC Navarro

  210), OFC Johnstun (220) and SGT McCaslin (200) were dispatched. Upon arrival,
  patrols spoke with CW2 Daniel Head

  ho stated that the individual entered the building with a backpack making
  concering comments. The bag pack was taken

  way and placed outside on the north side of the building and called the Police
  Station to report the incident SGT McCaslin

  equested K-9 to sniff the bag and the vehicle, a grey in color chevy Equinox
  plate #9MIN66 CA, for the odor of explosives.

  OFC Navarro and OFC Johnstun made contact with the individual, identified as
  Mr. Michael Snow (CIV/RET) from his

  Washington driver's license #WOL635SDD13B. Mr. Snow stated that he used to
  work in in the joint task force in the 80's

  while he was in the army. Mr. Snow also stated that he was threatened by
  cartels and that he needed to talk to someone about

  it. INV Olmos and INV Carison arrived on scene and requested the building #
  75025 to be evacuated due to the suspicious

  package. The building was evacuated and patrols secured both the entrances to
  the area. CHIEF Davidson also arrived on

  scene to assist. K-9 SPC Hayes (K-09) arrived on scene and conducted sniffs on
  the bag pack, the Chevy Equinox and

  building #70525, with negative findings. INV Olmos and INV Carlson transported
  Mr. Snow to the MPI office for further

  investigation. This is a final report.

  I
